I posted this the other day on comp.sys.dec and got no response.
Perhaps this group is more approriate.  I don't read this group,
though, so I'd much appreciate e-mail responses.

We're trying to implement a portable time class in C++ with some
specific requirements which make the existing classes we've seen
unsuitable.  We want to represent time in UTC wherever possible.
On VMS, gmtime() doesn't work because "VMS doesn't support UTC".
While that statement was true in VMS V5.2 or so when I added the function
to the VAX C RTL, I wonder whether it's still true.  I notice that
there's now some kind of a UTC time differential you can configure on
your system.  What kinds of routines are available to make use of that
value?  Do the routines handle daylight savings time properly?  How
would I use it to handle old UTC values which might have corresponded
to times when daylight savings time was in effect locally?

Any info would be appreciated.

Thanks!
